**What was exercised against the running build**

- **Positive:** On Mayo, a subcutaneous insulin bolus scheduled the glucose reminder every 120 minutes (trigger repeat 7,200,000 ms, job context interval 120) and fired with the exact 2-hour wording and no citation. An IV bolus kept the 60-minute schedule, hourly wording, and hourly citation. Subcutaneous then IV on one case shortened the interval to 60 minutes with the anchor unchanged. App launch 135 minutes after subcutaneous insulin alerted with the 2-hour wording. The changeset 245 backfill SQL, run by hand against seeded firings, flipped a subcutaneous firing to compliant and left the IV firing non-compliant.
- **Negative:** Glucose 65 minutes after subcutaneous insulin kept the scheduled rule silent. App launch at 90 minutes was silent. Demo tenant still scheduled at 60 minutes with hourly wording, so default sites are unchanged.
- **Red check:** Compiled the parent commit's four classes in the container, swapped them into the app, and restarted. The same Mayo subcutaneous bolus then logged a 1-hour reminder and the app-launch rule alerted at 90 minutes with the old wording. Restored the shipped classes (all eight checksums verified), restarted, and re-confirmed the 2-hour behaviour. The signature line appears exactly once in the container log, inside the swap window.

